    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia has contributed AUD4 million to the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC)&#x2019;s Protection of Civilians and Respect for the Law program in Papua New Guinea. ICRC is addressing issues of sexual violence and efforts include enhancing the capacity of local communities and healthcare facilities to provide care and support to survivors of violence. In 2022, 8 cycles of support sessions were provided for 97 people affected by sexual and other forms of violence, with 96% of participants reporting decreased distress after the sessions. Community outreach programs have reached 2,800 people with messaging aimed at preventing sexual violence.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
