   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s economic support to the Government of Vanuatu has provided funding to establish Vanuatu&#x2019;s PACER Plus Unit. Activities under this arrangement have included regional training for Customs staff, customs brokers and local producers around Customs, Rules of Origin, Regional Training on the Transposition of Tariff Commitments, and the &#x2018;Santo Export Gap Knowledge &#x2013; April 2024&#x2019; workshop. Collaboration with key stakeholders in the government and private sector has been a significant achievement in facilitating trade. This includes the Vanuatu Chamber of Commerce project where five local business have access to PACER Plus support to enable these companies to export. These businesses include Lapita Cafe Ltd, Vanuatu Beverage, Gaston Chocolat, 83 Islands and Tahun Kava Exports. Out of these five, Lapita Cafe Ltd has completed and received their certificate for manioc flour, enabling access to new markets in Australia and New Zealand.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
