    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT negotiated a policy reform matrix with the Government of Vanuatu as part of the Fiscal and Budget Support Package to support achievement of GoV reforms in the public finance, economic policy, and financial inclusion sectors. In 2021-22, with the support of DFAT, GoV approved the first National Financial Inclusion Strategy, 2018-2023, to increase access to financial services in Vanuatu. Building on this landmark reform, DFAT has continued to support GoV to improve opportunities for financial access in Vanuatu, namely for member-based organisations, with the Council of Ministers approving policies for the administration and supervision of credit unions in 2023.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
